Here is the commit message:
crypto: hisilicon/zip - save capability registers in probe
 process

Pre-store the valid value of the zip alg support related capability
register in hisi_zip_qm_init(), which will be called by hisi_zip_probe().
It can reduce the number of capability register queries and avoid
obtaining incorrect values in abnormal scenarios, such as reset failed
and the memory space disabled.

Fixes: db700974b69d ("crypto: hisilicon/zip - support zip capability")
Signed-off-by: Zhiqi Song <songzhiqi1@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the repeated querying of capability registers during the initialization process, which could lead to obtaining incorrect values in abnormal scenarios, such as hardware resets or memory space being disabled. This could result in the driver not correctly identifying the supported ZIP algorithms and capabilities, leading to potential failures in functionality.

